# Line-ending policy.
#
# Git on Windows defaults to `core.autocrlf=true`, which rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout.
# For most repositories that is harmless. Here it is not: tx402 hashes files and verifies
# signatures over their bytes, so a checkout that changes those bytes changes the hashes.
#
# The S13 cross-platform CI leg found this on its first run — the Windows job failed the
# TypeScript suite while macOS and Linux passed. Reproduced locally by converting a single
# vector to CRLF: `conformance:check` immediately reports the file as content-changed.
# Without this file, a Windows contributor cannot get a green checkout of a clean tree.

# Normalise everything to LF in the repository and on checkout, on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt and braces for the files whose *bytes* are load-bearing. `-text` tells git to treat
# them as binary and never apply any conversion, so no future `core.autocrlf` setting, or
# an editor's "fix line endings" button, can silently invalidate a hash or a signature.
#
#   - conformance vectors and their index carry per-file sha256 (SEC-007)
#   - the release manifest is Ed25519-signed and verified offline at client construction
core-spec/conformance/index.json          -text
core-spec/conformance/vectors/**/*.json   -text
core-spec/manifests/*.json                -text
core-spec/manifests/keys/**               -text

# Generated from the signed manifest by `tools/manifest-signer embed`; a test asserts they
# still match their source, so a line-ending rewrite would fail that test rather than
# corrupt anything — but there is no reason to let it get that far.
packages/tx402/src/core/bundled-manifest.ts        -text
packages/tx402-python/src/tx402/bundled_manifest.py -text

# Shell scripts must keep LF even if a checkout is otherwise CRLF: a CRLF shebang line
# makes the interpreter path unusable and the error message names a file that looks correct.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Lockfiles are tool-owned; keep them out of diffs.
pnpm-lock.yaml -diff linguist-generated
uv.lock        -diff linguist-generated
